{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>וְאִם לֹא קָרוֹב אָחִיךָ אֵלֶיךָ</b> — that he is not near you, for you are not obligated to go to another land with the lost item to return it to him, or you do not know him at all. And in the Sifrei (Ki Teitzei 247): \"I have only 'near' — from where do I derive 'far'? The verse teaches: וְלֹא יְדַעְתּוֹ.\" If so, the verse says: וְאִם לֹא קָרוֹב אָחִיךָ אֵלֶיךָ — in your city, such that you would inquire about him and know him; יִהְיֶה עִמְּךָ — until your brother seeks it."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "The Sifrei citation uses the section name תצא (Ki Teitzei); the numeral מז (47) refers to the comment's sequential number within that section in standard editions."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:53:06.142907400Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}